---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Terms" description="Terms of use for the Telfer Family Wiki — how you may use the information on this site and what to ask before reusing it." canonicalPath="/terms">
  <main class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-8">
    <article class="prose prose-lg dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
      <h1 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-[var(--color-heading)] mb-2">Terms of Use</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)] mb-8">The simple rules for using this site</p>

      <p class="mb-6">
        By using the Telfer Wiki you agree to these terms. They're intentionally short and written in plain
        language — there are no hidden clauses. If anything here is unclear, just ask.
      </p>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-heading)]">What You Can Do</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-2">
          <li><strong>Browse freely.</strong> All the information on this site is here for you to read and explore — no account, no sign-up, no cost.</li>
          <li><strong>Share links.</strong> Feel free to share pages with family and friends.</li>
          <li><strong>Print and save.</strong> You're welcome to print pages or save them for your own family records.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-heading)]">Copyright and Reuse</h2>
        <p>
          The text, photographs, and research on this site are the work of the family and its contributors,
          and are protected by copyright. The underlying genealogical facts (names, dates, places) are
          historical record, but our photos, writing, and research notes are ours.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          If you'd like to reuse a photo, quote a story, or use our written material in a book, article, or
          website, that's usually fine — just <a href="/contact">ask us first</a>. For personal family use,
          you generally don't need to ask; for anything public or published, please get in touch.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-heading)]">Sourced From Public Records</h2>
        <p>
          Family history is assembled from public records — birth, marriage and death certificates,
          census returns, newspapers, immigration and church records, reunion booklets, and family-provided documents. We combine and cross-check these sources, but genealogical research is
          never perfect.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          We aim for accuracy and we verify as much as we can, but we can't guarantee that every detail is
          error-free. If you find something wrong, please <a href="/contact">let us know</a> so we can fix it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-heading)]">Respect for Living Relatives</h2>
        <p>
          Living family members are treated with care: only the facts needed to hold the tree together are
          published, and some pages are kept out of search results. Please treat living relatives' information
          — and the people themselves — with the same respect when you share this site.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-heading)]">No Warranty, No Liability</h2>
        <p>
          This site is provided "as is" for family and general historical interest. We do our best to keep it
          accurate and available, but we accept no liability for any errors or omissions, or for any use you
          make of the information.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-heading)]">Governing Law</h2>
        <p>
          This site is run from Australia, and these terms are governed by the laws of Queensland, Australia.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-10">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-heading)]">Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these terms, or the site in general, are welcome — use our <a href="/contact">Contact page</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)] italic mt-8">
        Last updated August 2026. Terms of use for telferwiki.com.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
